{"name":"Moonless Night","hex":"#3c393d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moonless","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["During which no phase of the Moon is visible to provide light, whether because of cloud cover or because of a new moon.","Having no natural satellite."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moonless"},{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Moonless Night","blocks":[{"text":"A Moonless Night is a 2014 drama film written and directed by Germán Tejeira. The film was selected as the Uruguayan entry for the Best Foreign Language Film at the 88th Academy Awards but it was not nominated."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e7/A_Moonless_Night_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Moonless_Night","wikidata":"Q18416997"},{"title":"New moon","blocks":[{"text":"In astronomy, the new moon is the first lunar phase, when the Moon and Sun have the same ecliptic longitude. At this phase, the lunar disk is not visible to the naked eye, except when it is silhouetted against the Sun during a solar eclipse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/New_Moon.jpg/330px-New_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_moon","wikidata":"Q108566"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Una_noche_sin_luna_English.jpg/500px-Una_noche_sin_luna_English.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Una_noche_sin_luna_English.jpg/500px-Una_noche_sin_luna_English.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Connection between the three episodes in the film","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUna_noche_sin_luna_English.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Amavasya_and_Prathama_tithi.jpg/500px-Amavasya_and_Prathama_tithi.jpg?utm_sou